course: dictionary
lesson: 5370
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Kiwi is a good example. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The kiwi of New Zealand is a flightless night bird» is about an animal, because flightless and night describe a bird.
explain: Look for clue words. Kiwi fruit is a fruit, so you will read about skin, flesh and seeds. A Kiwi with a capital K is a person, so the sentence will be about someone, such as «Tama from New Zealand» saying «chur», a Kiwi way to say cheers.
explain: Always test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «A kiwi is a flightless night fruit»: it does not make sense, so the bird meaning is right. Read the whole sentence, not just one word.
fact: A kiwi is a small brown bird from New Zealand that cannot fly.
fact: A kiwi hunts at night and has nostrils at the tip of its long beak.
fact: Kiwi fruit is an oval fruit with brown hairy skin, bright green flesh and tiny black seeds.
fact: A Kiwi with a capital K is an informal word for a person from New Zealand.
fact: Kiwi fruit is a healthy snack, rich in vitamin C, and the kiwi bird is the national symbol of New Zealand.
exercise: «Not all birds can fly: penguins, ostriches, emus and kiwis are birds that can't, but all birds have feathers.» In this sentence, what is a kiwi? | *A bird that cannot fly | A person from New Zealand | A fruit with bright green flesh
exercise: «The kiwi comes out at night and finds worms by smell.» What does kiwi mean here? | A fruit with tiny black seeds | A brown hairy ball | *A bird that hunts at night | A person from New Zealand
exercise: Tama from New Zealand says «chur», a Kiwi way to say cheers. What does Kiwi with a capital K mean here? | A small brown bird | A type of drink | An oval fruit | *A person from New Zealand
test: Which kiwi has brown hairy skin, bright green flesh and tiny black seeds? | A small brown bird | A Kiwi, a person from New Zealand | *Kiwi fruit
test: In «a flightless night bird», what does flightless mean? | *Cannot fly | Full of light | Very fast | Sleepy
exam: Jayden reads «The kiwi of New Zealand has nostrils at the tip of its beak.» Which meaning is right, and why? | The person, because a Kiwi is a person | *The bird, because nostrils and beaks belong to an animal | The snack, because it is healthy | The fruit, because fruit has seeds
